+/*
+ * Package 3.0 doc 36 ("Editor Shell Master Layout") density rules for the
+ * open-project shell, layered on top of shell-controls.css rather than
+ * replacing it.
+ *
+ * The problem this file exists to solve: shell-controls.css gives every
+ * `.arq-shell-button` a 44px minimum in both axes, which is correct and
+ * non-negotiable for touch (blueprint section 121, and doc 36's own "minimum
+ * 44px touch hit target"). But doc 36 also specifies a 40px tab strip and a
+ * 38px context bar, and a 44px control cannot fit in a 40px strip. Both numbers
+ * are right for their own input; they are simply not right at the same time.
+ *
+ * So the relaxation is scoped to `(pointer: fine)` - a mouse or trackpad, where
+ * doc 36 specifies a "Desktop icon hitbox: 36-40 px" instead. A coarse pointer
+ * never enters these blocks and keeps the full 44px, which means a touch device
+ * gets a slightly taller strip than the desktop baseline rather than a target
